.nh
.TH "PB-SEND-LIST" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-send-list - List file transfers


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb send list [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List file transfers

.PP
List outgoing transfer batches, optionally limited by machine, terminal session, or result count. Use a returned transfer ID with status or cancel.

.PP
Send publishes a batch to a machine's Paperboat Inbox. Completion means the receiver verified and recorded the files; status and cancel act on a transfer ID. A default destination can be set separately, while --to chooses one for the current send.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for list

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON

.PP
\fB--limit\fP=50
	maximum transfers to return

.PP
\fB--offset\fP=0
	continue at a transfer history offset

.PP
\fB--on\fP=""
	destination machine name or ID

.PP
\fB--q\fP=""
	filter by file basename or transfer ID

.PP
\fB--session\fP=""
	terminal session ID for destination context

.PP
\fB--state\fP=""
	filter by transfer state


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-send(1)\fP
